the migration rewrites.\n\nKey consideration: the migration converts natural language trigger terms like 「派发 subagent」「SPAWN Sub Agent」「子 Agent」「父 Agent」「Main Agent / Sub Agent」 etc. into `workflowScript` + `runs.run`/`runs.all` + `agent:'worker'` etc. So after migration, these natural terms should significantly decrease. But some might remain as descriptive text (e.g., \"父 Agent 验收\" might remain to describe human review). Actually the KR3.3 says \"自然语言触发词显著下降\" (significantly decrease). And the acceptance says \"迁移后自然语言触发词计数 < 基线\" (strictly less than baseline).\n\nBut wait — there's a subtlety. The migration ADDS `workflowScript` examples and `agent:'worker'` etc. But the natural-language terms might still partially remain (e.g., \"父 Agent\" in the sense of orchestrator). The acceptance is just \"count < baseline\", not \"= 0\". So any decrease suffices.\n\nNow, an important risk: if I pick a regex too broad (e.g., just \"subagent\" case-insensitive), the migration's added `runs.run('main', {agent:'worker', task:'...'})` text might actually contain \"subagent\"? No. But `workflowScript` examples might include words like \"subagent\" in comments? Unlikely. But the migration might also introduce the word \"subagent\" in describing the tool (e.g., \"subagent 工具\", \"subagent 工具允许...\"). Actually, the migrated text will likely describe things like \"编排权在 parent、普通子 agent 不持 subagent 工具\". This ADDS \"subagent\" occurrences!\n\nThis is a real concern. The migration must add explicit \"subagent\" tool references (per KR3.3: \"普通子 agent 不持 subagent 工具\"). So the word \"subagent\" might INCREASE or stay, not decrease.\n\nLet me look at what the migration would actually do. The KR3.3 says: \"把各命令模板中自然语言 subagent 触发词...改写为显式 pi 触发语法\". The natural language trigger words like \"派发 subagent\" and \"SPAWN Sub Agent\" would be replaced by `workflowScript` examples. But \"子 Agent\"/\"父 Agent\" role names might be kept for describing who does what, or replaced by \"agent:'worker'\" etc.\n\nThe acceptance says: \"迁移后自然语言触发词计数 < 基线\". This is the key acceptance. So the regex must be chosen such that the migration (as it will be implemented) reduces the count. \n\nSince I'm writing the test script (RED phase), and the migration hasn't been done, I can't know exactly what the migration will produce. But I need to pick a regex that reasonably captures \"natural language trigger words\" — the phrases that ARE being migrated. The most specific phrases that will be replaced are the trigger imperatives:\n- 「派发 subagent」\n- 「SPAWN Sub Agent」\n- 「SPAWN Step N 子 Agent」\n- 「每个 Step 由父 Agent 启动一个独立子 Agent」\n- 「父 Agent / 子 Agent」\n- 「Main Agent / Sub Agent」\n\nActually, the safest approach: define the regex to match the EXACT trigger phrases listed in the task prompt and RFC, which are unambiguously \"natural language trigger words\" that the migration replaces:\n\n`派发 subagent|SPAWN Sub Agent|子 Agent|父 Agent|Main Agent|Sub Agent|subagent`\n\nHmm, but including bare \"subagent\" is risky because migration adds \"subagent 工具\" text.\n\nLet me think about what the migration adds vs removes:\n\nRemoves/replaces (natural trigger):\n- \"派发 subagent\" → becomes \"subagent({workflowScript: ...})\" or `runs.run`\n- \"SPAWN Sub Agent\" → becomes `runs.run(...)`\n- \"SPAWN Step N 子 Agent\" → `runs.run`\n- \"每个 subagent 独立启动\" → `runs.run`\n- \"父 Agent / 子 Agent\" role descriptions → partially kept as \"parent orchestrator\" / \"agent:'worker'\"\n\nAdds:\n- \"subagent 工具\", \"workflowScript\", \"runs.run\", \"runs.all\", \"agent:'worker'\", \"编排权在 parent\", \"单写者 one-writer\", \"普通子 agent 不持 subagent 工具\"\n\nSo the word \"subagent\" and \"agent\" will still appear, possibly more. The phrase-level trigger terms (派发 subagent, SPAWN Sub Agent) will decrease to ~0.\n\nGiven the acceptance explicitly says \"自然语言触发词计数 < 基线\" and \"显著下降\", I think the most defensible regex is one that captures the trigger PHRASES that get replaced, not the generic word \"subagent\". \n\nBut wait, the test method's own example regex for the pi syntax is: `grep -rcE 'workflowScript|runs\\.run|runs\\.all'`. And for natural language it just says \"以验收同一正则捕获自然语言触发词基线计数\". It doesn't give the exact regex. The task prompt lists 「派发 subagent」「SPAWN Sub Agent」「子 Agent」等.\n\nLet me reconsider: what's the best regex that:\n1. Is deterministic.\n2. Produces a meaningful baseline (matches the \"natural language trigger words\" concept).\n3. Will decrease after migration.\n\nI'll go with the phrases from N1 F1 (the authoritative source cited by RFC §2.1): 「派发 subagent」「每个 subagent 独立启动」「SPAWN Sub Agent」「Main Agent / Sub Agent」「父 Agent / 子 Agent」 plus related variants.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the count. The RFC says \"243 处：root 模板 134 处 + skills/ 109 处\". I found skills/ = 109 with pattern `subagent|Sub Agent|SubAgent|子 Agent|子Agent|父 Agent|父Agent|Main Agent|SPAWN` (occurrences). But root = 69 with same pattern, not 134.\n\nLet me look at what additional root-only terms exist. Let me check root templates for \"agent\" case-insensitive occurrences and \"subagent_1\" etc.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_7L3uN4xfyDKzwbKSHt4A2343","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== root templates list ===\" && ls internal/prompt/templates/*.md && echo \"=== per-file agent-ish terms (ci) ===\" && for f in internal/prompt/templates/*.md; do echo \"--- $f ---\"; grep -oiE 'subagent|Sub Agent|SubAgent|子 Agent|子Agent|父 Agent|父Agent|Main Agent|SPAWN|派发|Agent' \"$f\" | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; done"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":151,"output":1988,"cacheRead":34816,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1822,"totalTokens":36955,"cost":{"input":0.000065685,"output":0.00172956,"cacheRead":0.000126208,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001921453}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914512962,"responseId":"4f458c2d-4af8-4f37-acd1-aa5d0719a27d","