{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Hmm, my Python findall gives 176, but grep -P gave 109. The discrepancy is because grep `-o` with alternation and my regex `\\s*` etc. differ? Wait, actually the difference is that `findall` with a regex containing a single group returns... no, there are no capturing groups. Let me think.\n\nWait, `pat.findall` returns all non-overlapping matches. grep -P -o also returns non-overlapping matches. Why 176 vs 109?\n\nOh! I bet the issue is that `\\s` in Python matches more whitespace characters than grep's `\\s`. Actually grep -P `\\s` should match the same. Let me investigate the difference.\n\nActually wait, more likely: grep -o with alternation `SPAWN\\s+Sub\\s+Agent|...|Sub\\s*Agent` — when matching \"SPAWN Sub Agent\", the FIRST alternative matches \"SPAWN Sub Agent\". Then continues after. In Python, same.\n\nHmm, let me actually check: maybe grep -P doesn't support `\\s*` the same way, or the shell escaping. Let me recount more carefully. Let me list actual matches from Python."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_uOlo0Jrc3ikfZMyqSEHh7108","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re, os\nroot = 'internal/prompt/templates'\npat = re.compile(\n    r'派发\\s*subagent'\n    r'|SPAWN\\s+Sub\\s+Agent'\n    r'|SPAWN\\s+Step'\n    r'|子\\s*Agent'\n    r'|父\\s*Agent'\n    r'|Main\\s+Agent'\n    r'|Sub\\s*Agent'\n    r'|每个\\s+subagent\\s+独立启动',\n    re.IGNORECASE)\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter()\nfor dirpath, dirs, files in os.walk(root):\n    for fn in sorted(files):\n        if fn.endswith('.md'):\n            p = os.path.join(dirpath, fn)\n            with open(p, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                for m in pat.finditer(f.read()):\n                    c[m.group(0)] += 1\nfor k, v in sorted(c.items()):\n    print(repr(k), v)\nprint('TOTAL', sum(c.values()))\nEOF"}}}}
