{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Found it! `Sub\\s*Agent` with `re.IGNORECASE` matches \"subagent\" because \"Sub\" (case-insensitive) matches \"sub\", and `\\s*` matches zero whitespace, and \"Agent\" matches \"agent\". So \"Sub\\s*Agent\" ≡ \"sub\" + optional whitespace + \"agent\" = \"subagent\" with zero space!\n\nThat's the bug. I need `Sub\\s+Agent` (require at least one whitespace) to distinguish \"Sub Agent\" from \"subagent\", OR use word boundaries.\n\nSo the pattern should use `Sub\\s+Agent` (one or more spaces) instead of `Sub\\s*Agent`. Similarly `子\\s*Agent` — \"子Agent\" vs \"子 Agent\". Chinese has no case issue, `子\\s*Agent` matches \"子Agent\" and \"子 Agent\". That's fine (both are \"子 Agent\" variants). But wait, \"子Agent\" — does it appear? Earlier grep showed 子Agent: 0. So `子\\s*Agent` matches only \"子 Agent\" (28). Fine.\n\nBut `Sub\\s*Agent` must become `Sub\\s+Agent` to avoid matching \"subagent\". Let me also reconsider `Main\\s+Agent` — requires whitespace, fine. And \"SPAWN\\s+Sub\\s+Agent\" requires \"SPAWN\" prefix. Fine.\n\nAlso note: \"Sub Agent\" with multiple spaces? `\\s+` handles one or more. Good.\n\nLet me also reconsider: do I want to match \"SubAgent\" (no space, capital A)? Earlier grep showed SubAgent: 72 occurrences (but that was a different count including \"subagent\"? wait). Let me recheck. Earlier I ran:\n\n```\nfor P in 'subagent' 'Sub Agent' 'SubAgent' '子 Agent' ...; do grep -roiE \"$P\" ... | wc -l; done\n```\nResult: subagent: 72, Sub Agent: 26, SubAgent: 72, ...\n\nWait, \"SubAgent: 72\" — but grep -i \"SubAgent\" would ALSO match \"subagent\" (case-insensitive \"subagent\" contains \"subagent\" which... \"SubAgent\" pattern with -i matches \"subagent\" because \"sub\"+\"agent\" = \"subagent\" with no space). So SubAgent count = subagent count = 72. There's no actual \"SubAgent\" (camelCase) in the files; it's all lowercase \"subagent\". So I should NOT try to match \"SubAgent\" as a role name — there are none. The role name is \"Sub Agent\" (with space) or \"Main Agent\".\n\nSo my corrected pattern:\n```\n派发\\s*subagent|SPAWN\\s+Sub\\s+Agent|SPAWN\\s+Step|子\\s*Agent|父\\s*Agent|Main\\s+Agent|Sub\\s+Agent|每个\\s+subagent\\s+独立启动\n```\n\nWait, but `SPAWN\\s+Sub\\s+Agent` — the \"Sub\\s+Agent\" part requires \"SPAWN\" prefix, good. But there's also standalone \"Sub\\s+Agent\" alternative. Both fine. Note the alternation order: \"SPAWN\\s+Sub\\s+Agent\" before \"Sub\\s+Agent\" so \"SPAWN Sub Agent\" matches fully as one match (not counted twice). Good.\n\nLet me recount with the fixed pattern."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Y49UhL675P4mFNXuXikf9721","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re, os\nroot = 'internal/prompt/templates'\npat = re.compile(\n    r'派发\\s*subagent'\n    r'|SPAWN\\s+Sub\\s+Agent'\n    r'|SPAWN\\s+Step'\n    r'|子\\s*Agent'\n    r'|父\\s*Agent'\n    r'|Main\\s+Agent'\n    r'|Sub\\s+Agent'\n    r'|每个\\s+subagent\\s+独立启动',\n    re.IGNORECASE)\nfrom collections import Counter\nc = Counter()\nfor dirpath, dirs, files in os.walk(root):\n    for fn in sorted(files):\n        if fn.endswith('.md'):\n            p = os.path.join(dirpath, fn)\n            with open(p, encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                for m in pat.finditer(f.read()):\n                    c[m.group(0)] += 1\nfor k, v in sorted(c.items()):\n    print(repr(k), v)\nprint('TOTAL', sum(c.values()))\nEOF"}}}}
