{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now the Python count matches grep -P count: 109. \n\nSo the baseline (current, pre-migration) = 109 occurrences with this regex.\n\nNow let me finalize the design. I'm confident with 109 as the natural-language trigger count using this regex.\n\nBut wait, I should reconsider whether to include bare \"派发\" and bare \"subagent\". The RFC says 243 处. My regex gives 109. The difference (243 vs 109) is because the RFC's counting included bare \"subagent\" (72) and possibly bare \"派发\" (23+5=28) and \"agent\" etc. \n\nFor the test, what matters is internal consistency (baseline vs current using same regex). 109 is fine and meaningful. The acceptance \"显著下降\" will be satisfied because the migration removes most of these 109.\n\nHowever, I want to double-check the migration direction: will \"Main Agent\"/\"Sub Agent\"/\"父 Agent\"/\"子 Agent\" actually decrease, or will the migration REWRITE them but keep the labels?\n\nLet me look at the doing_loop and gen-loop and learning_loop to understand the current structure and predict the migration."}}
