My regex `\\d+` extracts 109. Good.\n\nNow, let me also double check the exit code and JSON: `print(json.dumps(result))` then `sys.exit(0/1)`. Ensure nothing else prints to stdout. The run() captures output (doesn't print). Good.\n\nOne more thing: subprocess with `text=True` and `capture_output=True` — for go test with `-v`, stdout could be large. That's fine.\n\nNow, potential issue: `os.walk(TEMPLATES_DIR)` — if TEMPLATES_DIR missing, os.walk returns nothing (no error). I handle the missing dir with a pre-check.\n\nLet me also think: the test method's pi syntax check counts FILES (`grep -v ':0' | wc -l`). My `files_with_match` counts files. Good. Same for agent names. For SENSE semantic check, the test method uses `grep -cE '...' sense_loop.md` which counts LINES (grep -c counts matching lines, not occurrences). Expected ≥1. My `len(SENSE_RE.findall(...))` counts OCCURRENCES, which is ≥ lines. Since expected is ≥1 and there are 16 lines/occurrences, either works. But to be faithful, I could count matching lines. Actually `grep -c` counts matching LINES. But ≥1 is trivially satisfied either way. I'll count occurrences (findall) — it's fine and arguably stricter. Actually, to be faithful to the test method, let me count matching lines for the sense check. Hmm, but it doesn't matter for the ≥1 threshold. I'll keep findall (occurrences) — simpler and the threshold is the same.\n\nWait, actually there's a subtlety: `grep -cE '批判门禁|反向回流|judgment.md' sense_loop.md` returns count of lines matching. If a line has multiple matches, grep -c still counts it once. My findall counts each occurrence. Both ≥1. Fine.\n\nNow let me also reconsider the trigger count semantics. The test method doesn't give the exact command for the trigger count; it says \"以验收同一正则捕获自然语言触发词基线计数\". So I define it as total occurrences. Fine.\n\nLet me also add to the script a clear header comment documenting the regex and the exact grep equivalence so the implementer can cross-check.\n\nNow, let me also verify: should I include `SPAWN\\s+Step` in the pattern? \"SPAWN Step 1 子 Agent\" — the \"SPAWN Step\" is a trigger phrase. But note \"SPAWN Step 1 子 Agent\" ALSO contains \"子 Agent\" (the \"子 Agent\" at the end). With finditer (non-overlapping), \"SPAWN Step\" matches first (position 0-10), then continues after \"Step\"... wait \"SPAWN Step 1 子 Agent\": \n- \"SPAWN\\s+Step\" matches \"SPAWN Step\" (indices 0..9).\n- Then scanning continues from index 10: \" 1 子 Agent\". \"子 Agent\" would match at the \"子 Agent\" position. So both \"SPAWN Step\" AND \"子 Agent\" get counted for the same line.\n\nIn learning_loop, \"SPAWN Step 1 子 Agent\" → \"SPAWN Step\" (1) + \"子 Agent\" (1) = 2 matches per line, 7 such lines → 7 SPAWN Step + 7 子 Agent. That's consistent with my earlier Counter: SPAWN Step 7, 子 Agent 28 (includes the 7 from SPAWN lines + others).\n\nIs this double-counting a problem? It's consistent between baseline and post-migration as long as I use the same regex. After migration, \"SPAWN Step 1 子 Agent\" becomes `runs.run('step1', {agent:'worker', ...})` — both \"SPAWN Step\" and \"子 Agent\" disappear. So the count decreases correctly. Fine.\n\nNow, let me finalize and write the file.\n\nActually, let me reconsider one more time whether to include \"Sub\\s+Agent\" as standalone. In doing_loop/gen-loop, the text has \"Sub Agent\" standalone (in \"Main Agent\" / \"Sub Agent\" headings). My pattern: \"Main\\s+Agent\" (21) + \"Sub\\s+Agent\" (24) + \"SPAWN Sub Agent\" (2). The \"SPAWN Sub Agent\" is a subset; with alternation order \"SPAWN\\s+Sub\\s+Agent\" first, it matches fully. Good. Total = 109 as computed.\n\nNow write it.\n\nLet me also think about whether `re.IGNORECASE` on `Sub\\s+Agent` could match something like \"SUB AGENT\"? Yes, but that's fine (still a natural trigger term). And \"main agent\" lowercase (3 occurrences) — the IGNORECASE makes \"Main\\s+Agent\" match \"main agent\". Good, those 3 are counted (in sense_loop/research \"main agent\" lowercase). After migration, \"main agent\" → \"parent orchestrator\"/\"main agent\" might remain? Actually sense_loop line 16 \"你（main agent）= sense 复核层\" — this \"main agent\" is descriptive and might be kept or changed to \"main agent\" or \"parent\". Hmm. It's only 3 occurrences. Even if kept, the overall count decreases.\n\nOK, writing now.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the PROJECT_ROOT computation once more and verify with a quick calculation after writing, by running the script.\n\nLet me write the file now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I now understand the codebase and the acceptance criteria. Let me verify a few more details before writing the test script."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_mDnzrp7JIICyXejtZjkV1344","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"=== current pi syntax files ===\" && grep -rcE 'workflowScript|runs\\.run|runs\\.all' internal/prompt/templates/ | grep -v ':0' | wc -l && echo \"=== current agent name files ===\" && grep -rcE \"agent:'worker'|agent:'reviewer'|agent:'think'|agent:'research'|agent:'exporter'\" internal/prompt/templates/ | grep -v ':0' | wc -l && echo \"=== sense_loop exists ===\" && test -f internal/prompt/templates/sense_loop.md && echo yes && echo \"=== baseline file exists? ===\" && test -f .rick/jobs/job_35/doing/trigger-baseline.txt && echo yes || echo no"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":153,"output":3890,"cacheRead":56832,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3638,"totalTokens":60875,"cost":{"input":0.000066555,"output":0.0033843000000000002,"cacheRead":0.000206016,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.003656871}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786914727170,"responseId":"df546401-4d22-4f53-881f-f5068297121f","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_mDnzrp7JIICyXejtZjkV1344","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== current pi syntax file